Z||000002||Cooter||03-19-2001||08:29 PM||||I hate to sound like an a$$, but I have that info here somewhere and can't find it. Try running a search on the 3.4 and see if it turns up what you need. It is here somewhere.||||reg||1
Z||000003||88formula||03-19-2001||09:52 PM||||The heads are the same so you can use either set. Use your fiero oil pan with the fiero front timing cover but you cal use either one. I used me fiero oil pan on my formula. You need an adapter for the oil pressure sensor and there is a boss that is missing on the 3.4 that you front engine mount bolts too. You have to make a bracket for it or buy it from Ed Parks. You also need a neutrally balanced flywheel or flexplate and you have re relocate the starter holes. You can find the rest of the information from these web-sites. <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html</A>   <A HREF="http://members.home.net/sprigint/x11p/engine/engine.html" TARGET=_blank>http://members.home.net/sprigint/x11p/engine/engine.html</A>   <P><BR>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 03-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfixit58||03-20-2001||07:39 AM||||Regarding the heads... The only difference in the cast iron 2.8 or 3.4 heads are the valve springs. If your installing the 3.4, use the 3.4 heads or, if the 3.4 heads are bad, use their springs (or buy new ones) on the 2.8.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
